KaizoCore patch to libretro/melonDS 66b5d2634cd0a79030562811e6e05f5532f800ba (GPL-3.0, as melonDS is): a savestate
brings the 3D engine's VertexNumInPoly back but not PolygonMode (melonDS saves the mode only in later versions), so a
state saved in the middle of a quad and loaded where the mode is triangles let SubmitVertex write a fifth vertex past
TempVertexBuffer, over NumOpaquePolygons among other globals. VBlank places the translucent polygons after that count,
so part of the list it sorts was never written, still null after a boot, and YSort read it: Black 2 resumed from its
snapshot closed KaizoCore (SIGSEGV at 0xd8, the polygon's SortKey; rc34's core at 0x11f130, the nightly's at
0x11b250). SubmitVertex now starts a new polygon instead of writing past the buffer, and VBlank counts the opaque
polygons from their own flags (and never sorts past the list). Neither changes anything for a game that was not
loaded from such a state. KaizoCore, 2026-10-04.

diff --git a/src/GPU3D.cpp b/src/GPU3D.cpp
index 9c02b2f..c833060 100644
--- a/src/GPU3D.cpp
+++ b/src/GPU3D.cpp
@@ -1424,6 +1424,15 @@ void SubmitPolygon()
 
 void SubmitVertex()
 {
+    // KaizoCore: TempVertexBuffer holds four vertices. A savestate brings VertexNumInPoly back but not PolygonMode
+    // (melonDS saves the mode only in later versions), so a state saved in the middle of a quad and loaded where the
+    // mode is triangles left VertexNumInPoly at 4 with nothing to reset it, and the next vertex went past the buffer,
+    // over the globals after it: in this build VertexNum, VertexNumInPoly, NumConsecutivePolygons, LastStripPolygon and
+    // NumOpaquePolygons. That count then left holes in the list VBlank sorts (Black 2 resumed from its snapshot crashed
+    // in YSort, rc34 and the nightly before it). Start a new polygon instead.
+    if (VertexNumInPoly > 3)
+        VertexNumInPoly = 0;
+
     s64 vertex[4] = {(s64)CurVertex[0], (s64)CurVertex[1], (s64)CurVertex[2], 0x1000};
     Vertex* vertextrans = &TempVertexBuffer[VertexNumInPoly];
 
@@ -2534,6 +2543,15 @@ void VBlank()
             {
                 if (NumPolygons)
                 {
+                    // KaizoCore: count the opaque polygons from their own flags. The translucent ones are placed after
+                    // NumOpaquePolygons, so when that count disagreed with the flags (see SubmitVertex) part of the list
+                    // was never written, still null right after a boot, and the sort below read it. Never past the list.
+                    if (NumPolygons > 2048) NumPolygons = 2048;
+                    u32 numopaque = 0;
+                    for (u32 i = 0; i < NumPolygons; i++)
+                        if (!CurPolygonRAM[i].Translucent) numopaque++;
+                    NumOpaquePolygons = numopaque;
+
                     // separate translucent polygons from opaque ones
 
                     u32 io = 0, it = NumOpaquePolygons;
